  },
  "body": "`bullet mission list` and `bullet mission status --mission <id>` now read the authenticated daemon through the existing validated atomic operator snapshot. Each invocation retains the original sequence, timestamp and source, refuses malformed or missing subjects, and uses the private credential store without opening a local ledger. Optional `--farmd` must match the saved destination.\n\nExplicit `mission status --data-dir <directory>` preserves local component inspection and rejects remote flags. Terminal output and errors use the existing control-character sanitization. Three actual CLI/HTTP fixture tests cover credentials, one read per invocation, malformed truth, missing missions, early subject/destination refusal and local-mode conflicts. The canonical inventory adds exactly those three identities (1,241 total / 1,195 standalone), with all prior identities and exclusions preserved.\n\nValidation: nine focused mission tests and strict Clippy passed; source, inventory and documentation have independent static review. The first full required run stopped at an existing backup test timeout (106 passed, one timed out); that failure is retained. The same test passed in 5.5 seconds in isolation under the unchanged fast profile. The full required rerun on current `e72325e64f112fd7b5be19b33bb0624bc922989a` passed: all 1,195 selected standalone tests, 34 contract tests, lint/inventory checks, security and documentation. The previously timed-out backup test passed in this full run under the unchanged policy. No assertion, exclusion or timeout was weakened.\n\nThese are authenticated component reads. They do not establish installed provider execution or change task submission, native controls, independent verification or release eligibility.\n",
